# K-quant type 114: Q6_K in 224-byte blocks (arcint's dword-aligned layout of the file's rows)

# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0003-0025. arcint 0.4.1 (DESIGN.md section 7.0.2bj).
#
# What changes:
#   fully_connected_kernel_kquant.cpp, fully_connected_kquant.cpp (ops), fully_connected.cpp
#                       (graph): a second Q6_K type id, 114, whose row is 224 bytes per
#                       super-block -- the file's 210 bytes then 14 zero bytes, laid out by arcint
#                       at load (--gguf-q6k aligned, its default) so every block is dword-aligned.
#   fully_connected_gpu_kquant.cl   KQ_TYPE 114 takes Q6_K's decoders at the 224-byte stride; the
#                       decode dispatch and the Xe2 prefetch as for 14.
#   kquant_utils.cl     kq_row_q6k_x: for type 114 the block is dword-aligned by layout, so the
#                       odd-block shuffle-down path of 0025 compiles out.
#   fully_connected_gpu_test.cpp   The host reference and the random blocks at the 224-byte
#                       stride; two correctness cases (type 114 at one row, and at nineteen 3-D);
#                       the timing test's two Q6_K shapes at type 114.
#
# MEASURED streamed at steady state (the timing test of 0023, every process warmed once, one
# row) against type 14 under 0025 in the same run, 2026-09-07:
#   24 GB card (Xe2):     down projection N 5,120 x K 17,408: 204 us (114) against 262 (14);
#                         N 1,024 x K 5,120: 27 against 27.
#   16 GiB card (Xe-HPG): down projection 247 against 260; N 1,024: 27 against 28.
# Correctness 16/16 on both cards. Served on the 24 GB card (mixed form, u8 KV, +p9 base, the
# file-row control in the same window): greedy outputs byte-identical at 856 and 71,727 tokens,
# Pruefstand 10/10 (17.0 t/s over its 1,145 tokens); prefill 531 t/s at 856 tokens against 418
# and 335 at 71,727 against 291 (the tiled variant's vector loads were paying for the 2-byte
# alignment too); the decode step 59.8 ms against 60.8 at 856 tokens and 77.7 against 79.9 at
# 71,727 -- the long-K down projections' gain; the K = 5,120 Q6_K shapes (the lm_head among
# them) are on the short-K dispatch and do not move. Resident 16.26 -> 16.54 GiB.

